  nonce: d210  # d210
  message: "Fixed in PR #275 (dev d7e9cdbe20). Root cause: _external_constructor_type's attribute branch required a bare ast.Name base, so a dotted-module constructor was structurally unreachable regardless of table contents; now unwinds the chain via _unwind_attribute_chain, which subsumes the single-segment case rather than sitting beside it.\n\nTHIS ITEM'S OWN HEADLINE FIGURE WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED. Filed at '41 primitives, BARE form only'. 29 of the 41 are django.db.models -- a MODULE, not a constructible type, so models(...) constructs nothing and no constructor fix can reach them; they already reach production via the .objects. dispatch (WI-sozoj, 447 filter + 121 get chains on pretix). The reach probe scored a call form that cannot exist in real code. Honest scope: 12 primitives across 4 types (http.client.HTTPConnection/HTTPSConnection, http.server.HTTPServer, xmlrpc.server.SimpleXMLRPCServer).\n\nREAL-CODE FLOOR (scripts/measure-dotted-ctor-floor.py, in-repo), over the 103 corpus files naming these types, counting only the joined ctor->catalogued-method shape: dotted 10 production / 21 test; bare 4 production / 13 test. The dotted form is the MORE common of the two for these types. Ten production sites, all net_send: mitmproxy release scripts x2, envoy socket_passing, ceph barbican, ClickHouse CI.\n\nDIRECTION A/B, 8 repos (scripts/measure-dotted-ctor-resolution-ab.py, in-repo): 60 call edges retyped, 0 lost, 0 net edge-count change -- the same edges moving external.<method> -> <Type>.<method>. mitmproxy 10, ClickHouse 38, ceph 8, envoy 3, sherpa-onnx 1. Neutral controls django/pretix/kserve all 0/0.\n\nEND-TO-END, because a retyped edge is not yet a boundary: envoy 631 -> 632 chains, +1 net_send/http.client.HTTPConnection.request, 0 lost, each arm under its own fresh XDG_CACHE_HOME. ONE repo only; 30 of the 60 retyped edges land on a catalogued method, which is the cohort ceiling before the production/test split.\n\nRESIDUAL filed as INV-dulum: module_imports is file-scoped, so a local shadow still mistypes; pre-existing at depth 1, widened here. Pinned by xfail(strict=True)."  # d210
